# Public base URL of the deployed site.
# Used for canonical URLs, Open Graph images, sitemap.xml and robots.txt.
#
# You usually do NOT need to set this. The site works out its own origin at
# build time, in this order:
#
#   1. NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL          (this file — wins over everything)
#   2. VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL (Vercel sets it; the stable domain)
#   3. VERCEL_URL                    (Vercel sets it; this deployment)
#   4. http://localhost:3000         (local development)
#
# Set it explicitly once you have a custom domain, because that is the only
# case the automatic values get wrong — they would keep pointing at the
# project's *.vercel.app address.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://shahzaib.dev
#
# No trailing slash (one is stripped anyway). Remember that NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# values are compiled into the build, so changing this needs a redeploy —
# saving it alone does nothing. Never put a secret in a NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# variable: it ends up in the JavaScript the browser downloads.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
